{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nThe coordinator and fuse remain inert until non-create families route through them. Cutover must preserve independent work, explicitly defer matching plans, and prove the new fuse would not have prematurely stopped historical successful or partially successful jobs.\n\n## Outcome\nMake typed coordination authoritative for non-create families behind an internal per-family rollback selector, persist explicit deferral metadata, add the new endpoint-failure scoped fuse (retaining the blast-radius mass-mutation guard `classify.check_blast_radius`), and emit exact pass outcomes.\n\n## Plan\n1. Venue-gate verified-fake Cloud/DC summary behavior, then change the internal operation-family default from legacy to coordinator; never dual-send.\n2. Route update, delete, probe, clean-label, repair-property, and conflict plans through coordinator/fuse. Preserve successful effects and recover rollback by re-observation.\n3. Defer remaining matching plans with scope/reason/`retry_not_before`; let independent scopes continue.\n4. Preserve exact applied/failed/deferred/skipped/recovered tallies and nonzero degraded-pass signaling.\n5. Replay the sanitized 1,200-run completed GitHub Actions slice. Count only normalized terminal outcomes, never warning/grep text, and prove zero premature termination of observed successful/partial work.\n\n## Testing\nVerified-fake batches assert wire order/call ceilings/tallies/logs/exit. Historical replay names any counterfactual stop and blocks if it predates observed later success.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each non-create family has one coordinator route and one internal legacy rollback value with no dual-send.\n- [ ] Venue-gated Cloud/DC verified fakes pass before the coordinator default changes.\n- [ ] Matching remaining work is deferred with exact scope, reason, and `retry_not_before`, while independent scopes continue.\n- [ ] Applied, failed, deferred, skipped, and recovered tallies plus degraded exit status are exact.\n- [ ] Migrated families route failure fusing through the new endpoint-failure scoped fuse; legacy ad-hoc retry nesting is unreachable for them and the blast-radius mass-mutation guard remains in force.\n- [ ] Historical replay of the completed 1,200-run slice shows zero premature stop before observed successful or partially successful work.\n\n## Out of scope\nCreate coordination remains S4; final legacy removal remains S5.\n## Impacted sites (existing dispatch seams the cutover rewires)\nRoutes the S3 T1 coordinator + T2 fuse into real non-create dispatch behind an internal per-family selector; additive, never dual-send.\n- `applier.py` (**784 LOC — only 16 under the 800 cap; the cutover MUST NOT grow it past 800**): `apply` (:359), `_apply_batch` (:538), `_apply_one` (:727) are where non-create families dispatch today. Route them through `coordinator.coordinate(...)`; net-new wiring lands in the coordinator/dispatch-phase modules or a small new selector, NOT by inflating applier.py.\n- `batch_dispatch.py` (148 LOC): `delete_one` (:54), `_mutation_to_batch_dict` — the legacy compound-replay/rolling-breaker path retired for migrated families (unreachable for them, retained for create until S4/S5).\n- `dispatch_apply_phases.py` (694 LOC): `_call_with_retry` (:76) is the legacy ad-hoc nested per-call retry that becomes UNREACHABLE for migrated families (they fuse through T2's `pass_fuse` instead); phase dispatch carries deferral/fuse/exact phase outcomes.\n- `coordinator.py` `coordinate(...)` / `CoordinationReport` (S3 T1) and `pass_fuse.py` (S3 T2) — the entry points routed into; consumed as-is.\n- `classify.check_blast_radius` — the pre-existing blast-radius mass-mutation guard; a DISTINCT protection, retained in force and untouched (AC5).\n- Operation-family selector: the internal `legacy | coordinator` per-family default flips to `coordinator`; the `legacy` value is the internal rollback path (AC1), never a dual-send.\n- `tests/fixtures/reconciler/rp03_fuse_completed_slice.json` (new): the sanitized 1,200-run completed GitHub Actions slice; the replay counts only normalized terminal outcomes (never warning/grep text) and must show zero premature stop before observed successful/partial work (AC6).\n\nCreate coordination (S4) and final legacy removal (S5) stay out of scope.\n## Guard preservation on the coordinator route (G6)\n`coordinator.coordinate(ticket_plans, *, execute, locate, budget_factory)` is a PURE decision core (zero I/O, no clock); its injected `execute(plan, mutation)` closure is the SOLE side-effect channel and is invoked ONCE per mutation in dependency order. Every guard the legacy `_apply_batch` loop enforces is preserved by hosting it at the SAME point relative to each physical invocation — none is lost by routing through the pure core.\n\nPer-mutation guards → inside the injected `execute` closure, before it dispatches each mutation (identical ordering to the legacy loop at applier.py:658-662):\n- Lost-lease `abort_check()` (epic dust-troth-naval, applier.py:660): the closure calls the same `abort_check` FIRST, so a lost ref-lock lease still raises `ReconcileLockLost` before any coordinator-routed mutation issues.\n- HEAD-drift recheck (`_recheck_drift`, applier.py:697 via :662): the closure re-pins HEAD and runs the same benign-subject-tolerant drift check before each mutation; a hostile drift still raises `HeadDriftError` and aborts the pass. Head-pin state threads through the closure, not the pure core.\n- rebar-id audit provenance: the closure delegates each physical op to the existing per-call dispatch (`dispatch_one`), which stamps the `rebar-id:<local_id>` label (dispatch_one.py:153/:247) — per-mutation audit provenance is unchanged.\n\nBatch-precondition guards → run on the full migrated mutation set BEFORE `coordinate()` is called, fail-closed, exactly as `_apply_batch` does today (applier.py:631):\n- Cross-project safety guard (bug 626d, `_cross_project_targets` applier.py:231 via :631): the offender refusal runs before coordinate() issues any mutation; a cross-project target still fails the pass closed.\n- Blast-radius mass-mutation guard (`classify.check_blast_radius`): retained unchanged as a precondition — a DISTINCT protection from the fuse (AC5).\n\nThe pure core owns ONLY outcome bucketing, dependency ordering, scope isolation and re-observation recovery; all imperative safety I/O stays in the injected closure/preconditions. The legacy per-family route (`route_for` == `legacy`) retains the original loop verbatim as the internal rollback value (AC1), never dual-sent. To respect applier.py's 800-LOC cap (784 today) the execute-closure adapter + coordinate() invocation + outcome→manifest mapping land in a NEW module `coordinator_route.py`; `_apply_batch` gains only a thin per-family branch (guards stay resident as preconditions)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787658232538782001,"uuid":"42316a68-de6f-440e-9ed5-5237848cce3a"}